<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-01T07:54:00+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Sun, 01 Nov 2026 07:54:00 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Trump speaks to Netanyahu as US weighs fresh military strikes on Iran: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135415379.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US President Donald Trump spoke with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu about military options against Iran while considering diplomatic negotiations. Secretary of State Marco Rubio indicated ongoing talks but stressed the importance of addressing security concerns. Israeli officials have doubted Iran's willingness to abandon its nuclear program or halt missile production. The situation remains tense as military preparations are reported by US and Israeli defense forces.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/donald-trump-speaks-to-benjamin-netanyahu-as-us-weighs-fresh-military-strikes-on-iran-report/articleshow/135415379.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/donald-trump-speaks-to-benjamin-netanyahu-as-us-weighs-fresh-military-strikes-on-iran-report/articleshow/135415379.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-01T07:46:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135415605,imgsize-63456.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[IShowSpeed's October 2026 Expedia campaign offered creators $1 per 1,000 views to repost approved livestream clips, with an $8,000 campaign budget]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135411202.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[IShowSpeed's collaboration with Expedia provided a unique avenue for creators to monetize selected clips from their livestreams. Launched on October 14, 2026, this initiative had clear content requirements and paid creators $1 for every 1,000 views their videos garnered. With an $8,000 budget that quickly diminished, this campaign showcased fresh possibilities for revenue generation within the realm of content creation, focusing on highlights from a single livestream.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/ishowspeeds-october-2026-expedia-campaign-offered-creators-1-per-1000-views-to-repost-approved-livestream-clips-with-an-8000-campaign-budget/articleshow/135411202.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/ishowspeeds-october-2026-expedia-campaign-offered-creators-1-per-1000-views-to-repost-approved-livestream-clips-with-an-8000-campaign-budget/articleshow/135411202.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-01T01:26:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclos