/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135410267,imgsize-63204.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California real-estate executive sentenced for hiding debt while soliciting investments]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135397883.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a significant ruling, Sanjeev Acharya, the former leader of SiliconSage Builders, will serve 18 months in prison after misleading over 20 investors about the company’s dire financial status from March to October 2020. He obtained over $2.2 million without revealing substantial debt. The court's verdict included a restitution order of over $2.25 million, highlighting the imperative for honesty in real estate investments.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-california-real-estate-ceo-concealed-his-firms-financial-troubles-while-collecting-investments-that-left-more-than-20-people-2-2-million-poorer-a-federal-judge-has-sentenced-him-to-18-months-in-prison/articleshow/135397883.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-california-real-estate-ceo-concealed-his-firms-financial-troubles-while-collecting-investments-that-left-more-than-20-people-2-2-million-poorer-a-federal-judge-has-sentenced-him-to-18-months-in-prison/articleshow/135397883.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-01T05:57:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135398120,imgsize-1362906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Irish man walks 3,000 miles across US after 5% chance of recovery]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135311336.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><li