e><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135310149,imgsize-164237.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Canadian publisher with 25 million Facebook followers loses Meta claim over 2020 shutdown]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135395448.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Canadian online publisher suffered significant losses when Meta permanently removed its Facebook pages in 2020. The publisher, which had millions of followers, argued that this removal violated its business rights. Despite submitting numerous advertisements, many faced rejection for policy violations, which included misleading content. A court upheld Meta's decision, emphasizing its protection under Section 230 of the Communications Decency Act.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-canadian-publisher-once-had-25-million-facebook-followers-and-submitted-more-than-500000-ads-before-meta-shut-down-its-pages-in-2020-a-us-appeals-court-has-now-upheld-dismissal-of-its-conversion-claim/articleshow/135395448.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-canadian-publisher-once-had-25-million-facebook-followers-and-submitted-more-than-500000-ads-before-meta-shut-down-its-pages-in-2020-a-us-appeals-court-has-now-upheld-dismissal-of-its-conversion-claim/articleshow/135395448.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-01T03:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135395749,imgsize-1410560.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Former reality TV contestant faces £500,000 falcon dispute and appeal]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin